#
# Stand-in for rocminfo in CPU-only test runs (tools/rdna/rdna3/cpu_pytest.sh puts
# this directory first on PATH).
#
# aiter, imported through flash_attn by the Qwen4Exp AMD modules, runs rocminfo at
# import. The real one enumerates every GPU of the box, which initialises HSA on
# all of them and wakes the idle cards, and aiter raises KeyError for an arch it does
# not list (the gfx1030 of a V620-only box). The tests fake the architecture
# themselves, so one gfx1100 GPU agent is all aiter has to see.
cat <<'EOF'
ROCk module is loaded (cpu_stubs/rocminfo stand-in, no GPU was asked)
=====================
HSA System Attributes
=====================
==========
HSA Agents
==========
*******
Agent 1
*******
  Name:                    CPU (stand-in)
  Vendor Name:             CPU
  Device Type:             CPU
*******
Agent 2
*******
  Name:                    gfx1100
  Marketing Name:          AMD Radeon PRO W7800 (stand-in)
  Vendor Name:             AMD
  Device Type:             GPU
  ASIC Revision:           0(0x0)
  Compute Unit:            70
*** Done ***
EOF
